Permission Matrix & Access Control (User Management)
TC-UM-09: Menu Navigation Visibility Matrix
Test Scenario: Verify that menu navigation items are correctly displayed or hidden based on user roles (Superadmin, Admin, User).
Pre-conditions: Test accounts are registered, approved, and active.
Steps to Execute:
Log in sequentially using each test account:
Test Account A: Approved Regular User
Test Account B: Approved Admin
Test Account C: Approved Superadmin
Inspect the sidebar / top navigation menu.
Expected Result:
Regular User: Sees standard user menus (e.g., Dashboard, Profile, Own Tasks). User Management / Admin settings menu is completely hidden.
Admin: Sees standard user menus + User Management menu (Add/Edit Users, Approve Users). Superadmin System/Audit logs menu is hidden.
Superadmin: Sees all menu items, including full User Management, System Settings, Audit Logs, and Admin Roles Configuration.

TC-UM-10: Action Button Visibility and Enablement (UI Level)
Test Scenario: Verify action buttons (Add, Edit, Block/Unblock, Approve, Assign Admin) reflect role privileges on the UI.
Steps to Execute:
Log in as Regular User and attempt to navigate directly to the User List page via URL.
Log in as Admin and view the User List (containing User, Admin, and Superadmin entries).
Log in as Superadmin and view the User List.
Expected Result:
Regular User: Cannot access the UI page (redirected to 403 / Access Denied page).
Admin:
"Add User", "Edit User", "Block/Unblock User", and "Approve" buttons are visible and active for Regular User rows.
Edit/Block/Delete action buttons are hidden or disabled for Superadmin rows.
Superadmin: All action buttons (Add, Edit, Block/Unblock, Approve, Designate Admin/Superadmin) are visible and active across all accounts.

TC-UM-11: Server-Side API Endpoint Protection (Bypass Test)
Test Scenario: Verify that backend API endpoints enforce role-based access control, blocking direct API calls (e.g., via Postman or browser DevTools) regardless of UI controls.
Steps to Execute:
Log in as Regular User, retrieve the active session token/cookie.
Send a direct HTTP request to Admin/Superadmin endpoints:
POST /api/users/add
PUT /api/users/{id}/block
PUT /api/users/{id}/role (Designate Admin)
Log in as Admin and send a direct HTTP request to Superadmin endpoints:
PUT /api/superadmin/{superadmin_id}/edit
DELETE /api/superadmin/{superadmin_id}
Expected Result:
Server responds with HTTP 403 Forbidden (or HTTP 401 Unauthorized) for unauthorized requests.
No database modifications occur on unauthorized API calls.

TC-UM-12: Unapproved / Pending Account Access Block
Test Scenario: Verify that registered accounts awaiting approval are denied access to both UI and Server endpoints.
Pre-conditions: A newly registered account with status "Pending Approval".
Steps to Execute:
Attempt to log in using the Pending User account credentials.
Attempt to make authenticated API requests using any generated token/session.
Expected Result:
Login fails with message: "Account pending approval. Please contact an administrator."
All API calls return HTTP 403 Forbidden.
